AMEND rq-071, presently bound to sha256:8a915d8f6e8a3abe9e2287c615eb86bb2c34db8614a5c62c3b9bd8f084720342.
The file content is accepted unchanged. It is a logic-free wrapper that locates the repository root, transfers control to .githooks/check-ledger.mjs, and propagates that script’s exit status through exec.
The non-built delivery record is incomplete, however, because SHA-256 addresses the file bytes but not its executable mode. The current repository entry is mode 100644; on platforms that enforce hook executability, Git may ignore it.
Amend the non-built artifact descriptor and Ops placement contract to require:
1. exact wrapper bytes matching sha256:8a915d8f6e8a3abe9e2287c615eb86bb2c34db8614a5c62c3b9bd8f084720342;
2. executable mode 100755 where the platform represents POSIX mode;
3. installation at .githooks/pre-commit;
4. core.hooksPath configured to .githooks for the verification repository;
5. failure, never skip, if the mode or effective hook execution cannot be established; and
6. the required mode and installation path included in the content-addressed non-built delivery manifest, since the file hash alone cannot bind them.
The real-commit oracle remains the final behavioral proof that the installed hook actually fires. Its fail-closed behavior does not replace the need to describe and provision the executable artifact correctly.
Re-present the amended delivery descriptor for ratification. The wrapper file’s SHA-256 may remain unchanged, but the complete content-addressed deliverable record must change.
— Aaron Anthony Damiano, 2026-10-18

RATIFY rq-079 — I reviewed the complete ledger bar bound to sha256:d19a67a00542e83ee7027be78f3ac17121953e2c46976ad2fa5448323d0e804a.
The bar asserts only the ratified C-S7, LedgerEntry, ledger-interface, field-type, and rq-038=A requirements. It correctly:
- hashes the canonical JSON encoding of [seq, prev, kind, payload];
- canonicalizes object keys recursively while preserving array order;
- includes kind in the hash preimage;
- enforces the exact genesis rule;
- checks nextEntry purity and progression from the last entry’s sequence;
- verifies that chains are rooted at genesis;
- detects rewrites of every hashed field;
- admits only complete appended JSONL lines;
- rejects rewrites, deletions, and partial appended lines; and
- independently constructs the expected appendEntry results, verifies exact persistence and newline completion, and proves that existing bytes are not rewritten.
The target src/ledger.ts is correct under the previously adjudicated ledger layout. The rq-077 note-copy error is transparently preserved in the historical record and corrected by docs/decisions/2026-10-18-ws3-5-sitting-rq-077-note-and-duration.md; because rq-077 was an amendment request and conferred no authority, this provenance correction does not invalidate the fresh rq-079 ratification.
I ratify this file as the human-ratified, non-provisional module bar for C-S7.
— Aaron Anthony Damiano, 2026-10-18

I AMEND rq-088. C-S2 remains designated as the WS-3 demonstration control, and its rationale, disclosure, and post-demonstration lifecycle are accepted unchanged.
Before ratification, replace the shorthand expected verdict with the exact observable outcome under the reconciled OPS ledger-reader vocabulary:
- capability C-S2 is present with status BLOCKED;
- its module grader-runner has derived state built_unverified;
- no non-provisional bar or oracle supplies authority for C-S2;
- the capability must not read VERIFIED; and
- the module must not read verified, authority_not_demonstrated, stub, inherited_debt, or absent.
This is the precise meaning of Plan v1.1’s phrase “built_unverified — never VERIFIED.” Reissue the designation at a new content address before executing the live capability build or observing its results. The later FX-CAP assertion must require the exact capability status BLOCKED, not merely any status other than VERIFIED.
— Aaron Anthony Damiano, 2026-10-20

